{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":234154,"name":"CK","username":"CK-iRonin.IT","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/ck-ironin.it/{size}/5622_2.png","created_at":"2025-08-01T13:42:26.195Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI’ll be advocating for this until Cursor implements a proper deny / allow list, or a competitor will.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLack of a proper user-controlled deny and allow list invites a serious failure for someone! At least, it prevents much smoother flow!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe commands must go through a deny list first, then through an allow list.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMatch on deny list - immediate stop of a command.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo match on either list - ask user!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt’s much better than whitlisting all possible git commands except git add and git commit!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI want to deny \u003ccode\u003e*rm -rf*\u003c/code\u003e in any piping command but I’m fine with single \u003ccode\u003erm\u003c/code\u003e .\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI want to deny \u003ccode\u003e*console* \u003c/code\u003eso it does not run any f console ever again!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese MUST be project specific - when I’m developing in a dev container with git the risk of catastrophic failure is super low, it’s opposite when I do a quick thing on my host machine.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":8,"updated_at":"2026-04-29T07:50:47.910Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":78,"reads":47,"readers_count":46,"score":489.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":124977,"topic_slug":"lack-of-denylist-will-bite-someone-sooner-or-later-give-users-control","display_username":"CK","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/your-ai-assistant-completely-deleted-all-my-files-from-my-computer/158182/8","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"Your AI assistant completely deleted all my files from my computer","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"raw":"I’ll be advocating for this until Cursor implements a proper deny / allow list, or a competitor will. \n\nLack of a proper user-controlled deny and allow list invites a serious failure for someone! At least, it prevents much smoother flow!\n\nThe commands must go through a deny list first, then through an allow list. \n\nMatch on deny list - immediate stop of a command.\n\nNo match on either list - ask user!\n\nIt’s much better than whitlisting all possible git commands except git add and git commit!\n\nI want to deny `*rm -rf*` in any piping command but I’m fine with single `rm` .\n\nI want to deny `*console* `so it does not run any f console ever again!\n\nThese MUST be project specific - when I’m developing in a dev container with git the risk of catastrophic failure is super low, it’s opposite when I do a quick thing on my host machine.","actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":6}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":7917,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/lack-of-denylist-will-bite-someone-sooner-or-later-give-users-control/124977/1","reactions":[{"id":"+1","type":"emoji","count":3},{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":3}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":6,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":true},{"id":234275,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2025-08-01T15:51:51.589Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the feedback, we’ll consider it.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":8,"updated_at":"2025-08-01T15:51:51.589Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":44,"readers_count":43,"score":38.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":124977,"topic_slug":"lack-of-denylist-will-bite-someone-sooner-or-later-give-users-control","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"raw":"Hey, thanks for the feedback, we’ll consider it.","actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":2}],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/lack-of-denylist-will-bite-someone-sooner-or-later-give-users-control/124977/2","reactions":[{"id":"+1","type":"emoji","count":1},{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":2,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":234276,"name":"CK","username":"CK-iRonin.IT","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/ck-ironin.it/{size}/5622_2.png","created_at":"2025-08-01T15:52:47.339Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eDeny list commands should simply be skipped by the agent or the step where Cursor asks user what to do abotu a command. Simple and improves the flow.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":3,"post_type":1,"posts_count":8,"updated_at":"2025-08-01T15:52:47.339Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":2,"reads":41,"readers_count":40,"score":63.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":124977,"topic_slug":"lack-of-denylist-will-bite-someone-sooner-or-later-give-users-control","display_username":"CK","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"raw":"Deny list commands should simply be skipped by the agent or the step where Cursor asks user what to do abotu a command. Simple and improves the flow.","actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":7917,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/lack-of-denylist-will-bite-someone-sooner-or-later-give-users-control/124977/3","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":362146,"name":"Frédéric G.-Boutin","username":"fboutin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/fboutin/{size}/102532_2.png","created_at":"2026-03-20T12:43:12.079Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI’ve got an example here. I started using the AWS MCP tool and it really only wrap calls around the AWS CLI command already installed and running locally. What I see is that sometimes the agent ignore the MCP and want to run the AWS CLI straight up.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe MCP allows for some safeguards, like specifying the AWS “profile” to use for all requests. In that situation, I explicitly gave a limited profile to the MCP for the Agent to use but when the Agent launches the AWS CLI directly it puts whatever it wants as a `–profile` switch, completely overpassing the MCP limitation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSo, this morning I wanted to simply “deny” Cursor the whole `aws` CLI command only to find out that… I cannot. There is no Deny list anymore.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat are we supposed to do?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":4,"post_type":1,"posts_count":8,"updated_at":"2026-03-20T12:45:47.240Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":7,"readers_count":6,"score":26.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":124977,"topic_slug":"lack-of-denylist-will-bite-someone-sooner-or-later-give-users-control","display_username":"Frédéric G.-Boutin","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"raw":"I’ve got an example here. I started using the AWS MCP tool and it really only wrap calls around the AWS CLI command already installed and running locally. What I see is that sometimes the agent ignore the MCP and want to run the AWS CLI straight up.\n\nThe MCP allows for some safeguards, like specifying the AWS “profile” to use for all requests. In that situation, I explicitly gave a limited profile to the MCP for the Agent to use but when the Agent launches the AWS CLI directly it puts whatever it wants as a \\`–profile\\` switch, completely overpassing the MCP limitation.\n\nSo, this morning I wanted to simply “deny” Cursor the whole \\`aws\\` CLI command only to find out that… I cannot. There is no Deny list anymore.\n\nWhat are we supposed to do?","actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":107047,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/lack-of-denylist-will-bite-someone-sooner-or-later-give-users-control/124977/4","reactions":[{"id":"heavy_plus_sign","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":362210,"name":"CK","username":"CK-iRonin.IT","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/ck-ironin.it/{size}/5622_2.png","created_at":"2026-03-20T13:30:52.839Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI switch to other solution that support hooks before running a command- I can have granural control over commands and their paramenters per directory.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":8,"updated_at":"2026-03-20T13:30:52.839Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":4,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":7,"readers_count":6,"score":21.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":124977,"topic_slug":"lack-of-denylist-will-bite-someone-sooner-or-later-give-users-control","display_username":"CK","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":107047,"username":"fboutin","name":"Frédéric G.-Boutin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/fboutin/{size}/102532_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"raw":"I switch to other solution that support hooks before running a command- I can have granural control over commands and their paramenters per directory.","actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":7917,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/lack-of-denylist-will-bite-someone-sooner-or-later-give-users-control/124977/5","reactions":[{"id":"+1","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":388443,"name":"","username":"alejo4373","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/a/c77e96/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-04-28T16:41:18.538Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/ck-ironin.it\"\u003e@CK-iRonin.IT\u003c/a\u003e  Can you elaborate? What does your setup look like?.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI had the same issue that Frédéric had. I have an MCP for Postgres, and I set it up in read-only mode. Then I asked Cursor to try to delete a record from the database. It attempted to work with the MCP, but due to the restriction, it failed. Then it wrote a sql script, got my ENV variable for the DB and called psql directly, and that succeeded. If I cannot prevent Cursor from calling any random command on my computer I’m really worried\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":8,"updated_at":"2026-04-28T16:41:33.593Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":5,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":7,"readers_count":6,"score":21.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":124977,"topic_slug":"lack-of-denylist-will-bite-someone-sooner-or-later-give-users-control","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":7917,"username":"CK-iRonin.IT","name":"CK","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/ck-ironin.it/{size}/5622_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"raw":"@CK-iRonin.IT  Can you elaborate? What does your setup look like?.\n\nI had the same issue that Frédéric had. I have an MCP for Postgres, and I set it up in read-only mode. Then I asked Cursor to try to delete a record from the database. It attempted to work with the MCP, but due to the restriction, it failed. Then it wrote a sql script, got my ENV variable for the DB and called psql directly, and that succeeded. If I cannot prevent Cursor from calling any random command on my computer I'm really worried","actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":113655,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/lack-of-denylist-will-bite-someone-sooner-or-later-give-users-control/124977/6","reactions":[{"id":"+1","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":388459,"name":"","username":"alejo4373","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/a/c77e96/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-04-28T17:10:31.064Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eWondering about \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/ck-ironin.it\"\u003e@CK-iRonin.IT\u003c/a\u003e setup, came up with this: \u003ca href=\"https://gist.github.com/alejo4373/ea9bc4dc47c0d13ab64a926b5e44019f\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ecursor-shell-command-logging-and-gating.md\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003etl.dr: Have a hook that runs on \u003ccode\u003ebeforeShellExecution\u003c/code\u003e. If the hook returns { “permission”: “deny”}, execution is prevented.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI asked Cursor to list the content of my directory using the \u003ccode\u003els\u003c/code\u003e command, and as the hook returned a “deny” it failed; it couldn’t do it. It tried to use Python, Node, and other runtimes to try to get the result, but it couldn’t. After that, I asked it to escape the hook to find a way. It tried a bunch of stuff, but couldn’t escape\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/fboutin\"\u003e@fboutin\u003c/a\u003e You’re probably interested in something like this.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":8,"updated_at":"2026-04-28T17:10:31.064Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":6,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":7,"readers_count":6,"score":26.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":124977,"topic_slug":"lack-of-denylist-will-bite-someone-sooner-or-later-give-users-control","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[{"badges":[{"id":109,"name":"Background Agent","description":"Helped a fellow community member solve their problem\n","grant_count":781,"allow_title":false,"multiple_grant":true,"icon":"user-group","image_url":null,"listable":true,"enabled":true,"badge_grouping_id":6,"system":false,"slug":"background-agent","manually_grantable":true,"show_in_post_header":true,"badge_type_id":3}],"badge_types":[{"id":3,"name":"Bronze","sort_order":7}],"basic_user_badge":{"id":130054,"granted_at":"2026-04-29T07:50:06.250Z","grouping_position":0,"badge_id":109}}],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://gist.github.com/alejo4373/ea9bc4dc47c0d13ab64a926b5e44019f","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Cursor: shell command logging and gating · GitHub","clicks":8},{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/your-ai-assistant-completely-deleted-all-my-files-from-my-computer/158182/10","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"Your AI assistant completely deleted all my files from my computer","clicks":2},{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/how-does-command-allowlist-denylist-really-work/102782/17","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"How does command allowlist/denylist really work?","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":113655,"username":"alejo4373","name":"","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/a/c77e96/{size}.png"},"bookmarked":false,"raw":"Wondering about @CK-iRonin.IT setup, came up with this: [cursor-shell-command-logging-and-gating.md](https://gist.github.com/alejo4373/ea9bc4dc47c0d13ab64a926b5e44019f). \n\ntl.dr: Have a hook that runs on `beforeShellExecution`. If the hook returns { \"permission\": \"deny\"}, execution is prevented.  \n\nI asked Cursor to list the content of my directory using the `ls` command, and as the hook returned a \"deny\" it failed; it couldn't do it. It tried to use Python, Node, and other runtimes to try to get the result, but it couldn't. After that, I asked it to escape the hook to find a way. It tried a bunch of stuff, but couldn't escape\n\n@fboutin You're probably interested in something like this.","actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":113655,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/lack-of-denylist-will-bite-someone-sooner-or-later-give-users-control/124977/7","reactions":[{"id":"clap","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":388525,"name":"Frédéric G.-Boutin","username":"fboutin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/fboutin/{size}/102532_2.png","created_at":"2026-04-28T19:30:37.735Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"alejo4373\" data-post=\"7\" data-topic=\"124977\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/a/c77e96/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e alejo4373:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHave a hook that runs\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThat’s some great stuff and that’s probably the best we can do right now.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBut I think this massive workaround shows how Cursor is dropping the ball at the moment on this issue.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI recently needed to come back working with Claude Code and I had to properly setup my permissions/sandbox and it works very well. I think Cursor should do like Cursor does and piggy back on Claude settings; observing them.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre data-code-wrap=\"json\"\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-json\"\u003e{\n  \"permissions\": {\n    \"deny\": [\n      \"Read(~/.aws/**)\",\n      \"Bash(aws *)\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e","post_number":9,"post_type":1,"posts_count":8,"updated_at":"2026-04-28T19:30:37.735Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":7,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":8,"reads":6,"readers_count":5,"score":56.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":124977,"topic_slug":"lack-of-denylist-will-bite-someone-sooner-or-later-give-users-control","display_username":"Frédéric G.-Boutin","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"raw":"[quote=\"alejo4373, post:7, topic:124977\"]\nHave a hook that runs\n\n[/quote]\n\nThat's some great stuff and that's probably the best we can do right now.\n\nBut I think this massive workaround shows how Cursor is dropping the ball at the moment on this issue.\n\nI recently needed to come back working with Claude Code and I had to properly setup my permissions/sandbox and it works very well. I think Cursor should do like Cursor does and piggy back on Claude settings; observing them.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"permissions\": {\n    \"deny\": [\n      \"Read(~/.aws/**)\",\n      \"Bash(aws *)\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n\n```","actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":107047,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/lack-of-denylist-will-bite-someone-sooner-or-later-give-users-control/124977/9","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null}],"stream":[234154,234275,234276,362146,362210,388443,388459,388525]},"timeline_lookup":[[1,426],[4,195],[6,156]],"suggested_topics":[],"tags":[],"tags_descriptions":{},"fancy_title":"Lack of denylist will bite someone sooner or later - give users control","id":124977,"title":"Lack of denylist will bite someone sooner or later - give users control","posts_count":8,"created_at":"2025-08-01T13:42:26.134Z","views":380,"reply_count":4,"like_count":14,"last_posted_at":"2026-04-28T19:30:37.735Z","visible":true,"closed":false,"archived":false,"has_summary":false,"archetype":"regular","slug":"lack-of-denylist-will-bite-someone-sooner-or-later-give-users-control","category_id":5,"word_count":667,"deleted_at":null,"user_id":7917,"featured_link":null,"pinned_globally":false,"pinned_at":null,"pinned_until":null,"image_url":null,"slow_mode_seconds":0,"draft":null,"draft_key":"topic_124977","draft_sequence":null,"unpinned":null,"pinned":false,"current_post_number":1,"highest_post_number":9,"deleted_by":null,"actions_summary":[{"id":4,"count":0,"hidden":false,"can_act":false},{"id":8,"count":0,"hidden":false,"can_act":false},{"id":10,"count":0,"hidden":false,"can_act":false},{"id":7,"count":0,"hidden":false,"can_act":false}],"chunk_size":20,"bookmarked"